---
## Proposed answer:
To allow BGP-LS route exchange with peer `2001:DB8:2::2` in IPv6 address family, you need to configure the `advertise-ipv6-next-hops` command under the BGP neighbor configuration. Here are the appropriate CLI configuration commands:

```plaintext
config> router> bgp
config-router-bgp> group internal
config-router-bgp-group> neighbor 2001:DB8:2::2
config-router-bgp-group-neighbor> advertise-ipv6-next-hops
```

These commands enable the advertisement of IPv6 next hops for the specified BGP neighbor, which is necessary for BGP-LS route exchange in the IPv6 address family.
